<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa 1997 sunseed areas drops to 464,000 ha.</title>
<headline>S.Africa 1997 sunseed areas drops to 464,000 ha.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's National Crop Estimates Committee said on Monday the 1997 sunflower seed acreage estimate amounted to 464,000 hectares, well below 1996 plantings of 608,000 hectares.</p>
<p>But a spokesman for the committee noted the 1996 acreage had been much higher than normal. &quot;A lot of sunflower was planted (last year) in areas were it had become too late to plant maize due to rains,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He said the 1997 acreage could be raised when the next estimates were made. &quot;There were a lot of late plantings this year, and it may still increase.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
